            <ArticleTitle>A new upper bound of geometric constant [Formula: see text].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>203</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s13660-017-1474-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new constant [Formula: see text] is introduced into any real [Formula: see text]-dimensional symmetric normed space X. By virtue of this constant, an upper bound of the geometric constant [Formula: see text], which is used to measure the difference between Birkhoff orthogonality and isosceles orthogonality, is obtained and further extended to an arbitrary m-dimensional symmetric normed linear space ([Formula: see text]). As an application, the result is used to prove a special case for the reverse Hölder inequality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
